Z||000006||pherder||07-18-2001||09:51 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Bluebottlejunky:<BR><B>Artero has a nice a$$ looks like Diablo..but the face is ugly! Saw a yellow one at MI show</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The yellow one is John Good's Artero.  His is the second link (I believe).<P>Have you seen the front end of a real Diablo?  PISA (or whomever came up with this kit) got the front end to look as much as they could to a Diablo front end <B>WITHOUT</B> cutting the front end out of the Fiero's frame.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fieroburton:<BR><B>I plan to build one but need to save a lot of money first, but how much are you selling yours for ?<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Looking to get $3000 for the body kit.  Last I saw, PISA was selling the body, dash, lights, and some other pieces (which I can't remember or find right now) for $5000.  I have the Corvette tail lights already and they would go with the kit along with a set of driving lights for the front.<P>For $5000, I would throw in the 88 Formula (w/brand new 3.2 V6 ... 20 minutes cam break in time only on engine!).  The Formula is a 5 speed car with a solid roof w/new outer dew wipes installed (just got done doing them.)  The car has had the body kit loosely attached to it but the body has been removed to do some more work to the car it's self.  The body could be put back on to move it (i.e. trailer the car/body as one piece with the extra pieces not yet installed carried either inside the car or in the towing vehicle.)<P>Paul||||reg||1
